.policy "ruff-com818-trailing-comma-on-bare-tuple" revision 2
.description "Remove a stray comma at the end of a statement, or parenthesize the tuple; a trailing comma silently turns the value into a tuple."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff COM818 (flake8-commas): a comma that ends a logical line, which makes the statement's value a tuple
// without parentheses. Usually a typo: `x = 1,` binds `(1,)`. Ruff sees it in the token stream: a comma, then
// (comments skipped) the end of the logical line. That is a simple statement whose last token is a comma, with no
// `;` after it. Inside brackets the line does not end there. Reported at the comma.
//   foo = 1,                     ← COM818
//   bar = 1; foo = bar,          ← COM818
//   return False,                ← COM818
//   foo = (1,)                   not reported
//   foo = 1,; bar = 2            not reported: a `;` follows
#include "python/ast.rr"

.violation COM818(at: node) code "COM818"
    "Remove the trailing comma if a single value was meant; if a tuple is intended, parenthesize it as `(value,)`."
    suppress ruff "COM818"
// The bare tuple is an expression_list of one element, ending where the statement does; the tape stores no
// comma there, as the grammar implies it (RER-131), so the finding is on the tuple, and a `;` after it is the
// statement's next stored token.
COM818(x) :- (kind(p, "module") ; kind(p, "block")), child(p, s, _), node(_, s, _, _, e), kind(x, "expression_list"),
    node(_, x, _, _, e), (x = s ; within(x, s)), count : { child(x, c, _), !kind(c, "comment") } = 1,
    !semicolon_after(s).
.decl semicolon_after(s: node)
semicolon_after(s) :- token_after(s, u), text(u, ";").
